-- title:
--   Moduli places of a Γ₀(N)-class share their centre
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $N$ a nonzero natural number with $N \neq 0$ in $K$, and let $x$ be a point of [`ModularCurve.ModuliPoint N K`](def/ModularCurve_ModuliPoint.html#L35), i.e. a class of pairs $(E,P)$ consisting of a Weierstrass curve over $K$ with invertible discriminant together with a point of exact additive order $N$, modulo the relation generated by a variable change combined with replacing the marked point by a multiple $k$ with $\gcd(k,N)=1$. Let $F_N$ denote [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFullC K N`](def/ModularCurve_X0ModL.html#L100), the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,K\,d$ applied to the $q$-expansion $\tilde j =$ `jqModC K` for the divisors $d \mid N$, $d \neq 0$, and let $v, v'$ be places of $F_N$ over $K$ in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22): valuation subrings of $F_N$ containing $K$, not equal to $F_N$, and principal ideal rings. Assume both are moduli places of $x$, that is, each arises from some extension field $\Omega/K$ and some `ModuliTestDatum K N x Ω` $D$, with valuation subring equal to the preimage of $D.W$'s valuation subring under the $K$-algebra embedding $D.\mathrm{emb} : F_N \to \Omega$. Then for every $a \in F_N$ integral over the image of $K[\tilde j]$ — i.e. such that some monic $P \in K[X][Y]$ satisfies $P(a) = 0$ after evaluating the coefficients of $P$ at the element $\tilde j =$ `jModElt K (jqModC_mem_full K N)` of $F_N$ — the element $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $v$'s valuation ring if and only if it lies in the maximal ideal of $v'$'s valuation ring.
--
--   This says that two moduli places attached to the same $\Gamma_0(N)$-class have the same centre on the integral closure of $K[\tilde j]$ in $F_N$, the normal model of the modular function field over the finite $j$-line; the underlying geometric fact is that the $K$-points of this model over finite $j$ are exactly the $\Gamma_0(N)$-classes. It is the separation step used by [`ModularCurve.eq_of_isModuliPlaceOf`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eq_of_isModuliPlaceOf), which upgrades it to uniqueness of the moduli place of $x$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IsModuliPlaceOf_mem_nonunits_iff_of_isIntegral_jModElt.lean

import Mathlib
